    icon: '🃏',
  },
  data: {
    LLM: "1. **Bidding**: Starting left of the dealer, players bid for the right to 'Pitch' (name trump). Bids range from 1 to 5. 2. **The Kitty**: The high bidder takes the 5-card kitty and discards 5 cards to return to a 6-card hand. 3. **The Pitch**: The high bidder leads the first card; the suit of this card is trumps. 4. **Trump Hierarchy**: A (High), K, Q, J, Joker, 10, 9, 6 (Low). 5. **Trick Play**: Must follow suit if possible; else any card. Highest trump wins the trick; if no trump, highest card of led suit wins. 6. **Scoring**: At hand's end, count points.",
    Player: "1. **Bidding**: Starting left of the dealer, players bid for the right to 'Pitch' (name trump). Bids range from 1 to 5. 2. **The Kitty**: The high bidder takes the 5-card kitty and discards 5 cards to return to a 6-card hand. 3. **The Pitch**: The high bidder leads the first card; the suit of this card is trumps. 4. **Trump Hierarchy**: A (High), K, Q, J, Joker, 10, 9, 6 (Low). 5. **Trick Play**: Must follow suit if possible; else any card. Highest trump wins the trick; if no trump, highest card of led suit wins. 6. **Scoring**: At hand's end, count points.",
    objective: 'The bidding team must earn at least as many points as they bid. Points are scored for High, Low, Jack, Joker, and Game.',
    gameplay: "1. **Bidding**: Starting left of the dealer, players bid for the right to 'Pitch' (name trump). Bids range from 1 to 5. 2. **The Kitty**: The high bidder takes the 5-card kitty and discards 5 cards to return to a 6-card hand. 3. **The Pitch**: The high bidder leads the first card; the suit of this card is trumps. 4. **Trump Hierarchy**: A (High), K, Q, J, Joker, 10, 9, 6 (Low). 5. **Trick Play**: Must follow suit if possible; else any card. Highest trump wins the trick; if no trump, highest card of led suit wins. 6. **Scoring**: At hand's end, count points.",
    keyRules: [
      'High (1 pt): Winning or holding the highest trump in play (Ace).',
      'Low (1 pt): Winning or holding the lowest trump in play (Six).',
      'Jack (1 pt): Capturing the Jack of trumps in a trick.',
      'Joker (1 pt): Capturing the Joker in a trick.',
      'Game (1 pt): Winning the highest total value of pip-cards (A=4, K=3, Q=2, J=1, 10=10).',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: true,
