    setup: {
      players: '4 players in two partnerships (North-South vs East-West).',
      deck: '29 cards: Ace, King, Queen, Jack, Ten, Nine, Six of each suit, plus one Joker. Remove 2, 3, 4, 5, 7, and 8 from a standard deck.',
      equipment: 'Standard pack (modified), score sheet.',
      dealing: "Each player is dealt 6 cards in batches of 3. The 5 remaining cards are placed face down as the 'Kitty'.",
    },
    turnFlow: "1. **Bidding**: Starting left of the dealer, players bid for the right to 'Pitch' (name trump). Bids range from 1 to 5. 2. **The Kitty**: The high bidder takes the 5-card kitty and discards 5 cards to return to a 6-card hand. 3. **The Pitch**: The high bidder leads the first card; the suit of this card is trumps. 4. **Trump Hierarchy**: A (High), K, Q, J, Joker, 10, 9, 6 (Low). 5. **Trick Play**: Must follow suit if possible; else any card. Highest trump wins the trick; if no trump, highest card of led suit wins. 6. **Scoring**: At hand's end, count points.",
    moveValidityConditions: {
      ante: 'Arizona Pitch has no ante; it uses bidding for the right to name trump.',
