    exampleHands: [
      'Setup example: 6 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: The bidding team must earn at least as many points as they bid. Points are scored for High, Low, Jack, Joker, and Game.',
      "Turn-flow example: 1. **Bidding**: Starting left of the dealer, players bid for the right to 'Pitch' (name trump). Bids range from 1 to 5. 2. **The Kitty**: The high bidder takes the 5-card kitty and discards 5 cards to return to a 6-card hand. 3. **The Pitch**: The high bidder leads the first card; the suit of this card is trumps. 4. **Trump Hierarchy**: A (High), K, Q, J, Joker, 10, 9, 6 (Low). 5. **Trick Play**: Must follow suit if possible; else any card. Highest trump wins the trick; if no trump, highest card of led suit wins. 6. **Scoring**: At hand's end, count points.",
      "Scoring example: Pitch uses a 'Setback' scoring system where failing a bid subtracts from your total. Usually played to a target score of 21 or 31 points..",
